  "summary": "Five preprints in mid-November 2026 supply nonlinear, modified-gravity and field-level modeling tools for LSST Year 1 and DESI-class analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is theory and inference infrastructure for upcoming survey analyses. Hi-COLA trains an emulator for the nonlinear matter power spectrum in Cubic Galileon gravity, validated for LSST Year 1 weak lensing and clustering. bihalofit-JAX supplies a differentiable, open-source nonlinear bispectrum code with projected statistics, running orders of magnitude faster than existing approaches. A cubic-order EFT forward model for the Lyman-alpha forest, validated on CAMELS and Sherwood, yields BAO shift predictions and simulation-based priors. A physics-informed neural network reconstructs the dark energy equation of state and growth index from DESI DR2 and other data to test GR consistency. The QCD equation-of-state paper is more peripheral, addressing early-universe expansion, cosmological parameters and the stochastic gravitational-wave spectrum.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
